# AI Disclosure

## Concept

The overall **risk-management concept** — using a Random Forest vol forecast
plus a Gaussian HMM regime classifier plus per-state vol-targeting for
position sizing, validated with walk-forward and block-bootstrap — was conceived
and directed by the project owner.

## Implementation

The implementation (Python code, test suite, documentation, and pipeline
infrastructure) was developed with AI assistance. AI helped with:
- Initial scaffolding of the HMM + RF + per-state-target pipeline
- Iterative debugging and bug-fixing (notably the look-ahead bias and
  lookahead-via-vol-feature issues in earlier iterations)
- Statistical-significance analysis (t-test, Wilcoxon, binomial,
  Cohen's d)
- Documentation drafting and cross-checking

The project owner reviewed, directed, and made final decisions on:
- Pipeline architecture and config defaults
- Statistical-significance thresholds and what constitutes "honest" reporting
- What features to keep or remove (notably: removal of the Feng 2019
  worst-case feature after it provided no measurable benefit)
- Asset-class-specific transaction-cost assumptions
- Scope of multi-asset and Russell 2000 tests
